From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:53:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915: a repair of a sink's link shortly after a relink
 keeps the port off as well

Issue #28 (corgeone), after linux-9882: with Hades 1.2 the port kept off
before the link of an Anthem AVM 90 is set up again after a drop of its
HPD (an input switch, the AVM leaving standby) acts every time and mostly
brings the picture back, but not always, at hdmi_relink_off_ms=300 and
1000 alike. Every failure had the same pattern, and no good case had it:
a few seconds after the link came back with the port kept off (a relink;
2.2 s in the log he gave), a later look of intel_ddi_hotplug() (linux-9934, 9981) read the sink's
TMDS_Config as 0x00 again, and the repair modeset of
intel_hdmi_reset_link() went out with no time off, since 9882 keeps the
port off only before the first set up after HPD comes back. The AVM then
showed no picture until the output was turned off for 0.3 s and on again
from user space (Kodi's ToggleDPMS twice), which brought it back at once.
His log at 1000 ms (uptime in s): 2368.86 the relink; 2371.02 "Sink's
TMDS config 0x00 doesn't match the link (scrambling yes, 1/40),
modeset"; 2371.06 its mode set, and no picture.

So within 5 s (INTEL_HDMI_RELINK_WATCH_MS) of a relink, a repair modeset
of intel_hdmi_reset_link() keeps the port off first as well, as a relink
does: until it has been off i915.hdmi_relink_off_ms, and HPD back as long
where HPD came back again meanwhile. That is what the DPMS toggle does,
the one thing that worked every time. Each such repair is a relink and
starts the 5 s again; the cap of 3 modesets in 20 s still holds. For
those 5 s intel_ddi_hotplug() also goes on looking at the sink's SCDC
once a second, as it does after a look put off by a pending commit
(linux-9981, 14 looks after a hotplug at most), so that a reset after a
repair made near the end of the looks is seen as well. The kernel log
says each such repair, with what the sink reports of the link it gets
(SCDC 0x40 and 0x21: clock detected, channels locked, scrambling seen),
and how long the port stayed off.

Not taken: writing the sink's TMDS_Config again without a modeset
(upstream's comment in intel_hdmi_reset_link(): HDMI 2.0 wants the TMDS
clock and data suspended while the sink's TMDS clock rate changes, which
is why it makes a full modeset; and on this AVM a modeset with the clock
stopped for a few ms already failed in 1.1); and a later first look after
a relink (a longer wait before the repair, scdc_settle_ms=2000 in 1.1,
did not help, and the reset to repair is the sink's own, at a time of
its own).

Nothing changes where no relink came less than 5 s before: a normal
start, the mode sets asked by user space, a sink that never drops HPD, an
LG G5 whose drop answers a modeset of the output (no relink there).
hdmi_relink_off_ms=0 turns this off with the rest, as in 1.1.

KUnit (drm_hdmi_scdc_settle): the watch and the repair at its edges, the
failing case of the report at 1000 and at 300 ms, with HPD back again
meanwhile, the parameter off, and an LG G5's repair as before.

Not tried on hardware: corgeone can, with his DPMS service stopped, by
switching the AVM's input and by waking it from standby.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_ddi.c      | 96 +++++++++++++++++--
 .../drm/i915/display/intel_display_types.h    |  9 ++
 .../drm/i915/display/intel_hdmi_scdc_settle.h | 46 ++++++++-
 .../gpu/drm/tests/drm_hdmi_scdc_settle_test.c | 50 ++++++++++
 4 files changed, 189 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_ddi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_ddi.c
index 7901c9b..c57012e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_ddi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_ddi.c
@@ -3439,15 +3439,31 @@ gen9_chicken_trans_reg_by_port(struct intel_display *display, enum port port)
 
 /*
  * Hades: after a drop of a sink's HPD that no modeset of the output explains, the first set up of
- * the output keeps its port off until it has been off this long and HPD back this long
- * (intel_hdmi_scdc_settle.h); 0 turns it off
+ * the output keeps its port off until it has been off this long and HPD back this long, and so does
+ * a repair modeset of the link within INTEL_HDMI_RELINK_WATCH_MS after that (intel_hdmi_scdc_settle.h);
+ * 0 turns it off
  */
 static unsigned int hdmi_relink_off_ms = 300;
 module_param(hdmi_relink_off_ms, uint, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(hdmi_relink_off_ms,
 	"HDMI: ms that the port stays off before its link is set up again, after a drop of the sink's "
 	"HPD that no modeset of the output explains, such as an AV receiver switching inputs or "
-	"leaving standby (default 300, 0: as before; at most 2000)");
+	"leaving standby, and before a repair of that link in the 5 s after it (default 300, 0: as "
+	"before; at most 2000)");
+
+/*
+ * Hades: ms since the output was last set up after its port was kept off (intel_hdmi_relink_off());
+ * -1 where it never was, or INTEL_HDMI_RELINK_WATCH_MS or more ago
+ */
+static long intel_hdmi_since_relink(struct intel_connector *connector)
+{
+	const unsigned long at = READ_ONCE(connector->relinked_at);
+
+	if (!READ_ONCE(connector->relinked) ||
+	    time_after_eq(jiffies, at + msecs_to_jiffies(INTEL_HDMI_RELINK_WATCH_MS)))
+		return -1;
+	return jiffies_to_msecs(jiffies - at);
+}
 
 /* Hades: i915.hdmi_relink_off_ms, before intel_ddi_enable_hdmi() sets the link up */
 static void intel_hdmi_relink_off(struct intel_connector *connector)
@@ -3457,15 +3473,21 @@ static void intel_hdmi_relink_off(struct intel_connector *connector)
 				       INTEL_HDMI_RELINK_OFF_MAX_MS);
 	const unsigned long back_at = connector->hpd_back_at;
 	const unsigned long off_at = READ_ONCE(connector->output_off_at);
-	unsigned int since_back, since_off = UINT_MAX, wait;
+	const bool drop = READ_ONCE(connector->relink_off_due);
+	const bool repair = READ_ONCE(connector->relink_repair_due);
+	unsigned int since_back = UINT_MAX, since_off = UINT_MAX, wait;
 
-	if (!READ_ONCE(connector->relink_off_due))
+	if (!drop && !repair)
 		return;
 	WRITE_ONCE(connector->relink_off_due, false);
+	WRITE_ONCE(connector->relink_repair_due, false);
+	if (!off)
+		return;
 	/* (a set up long after HPD came back is not the one of that hotplug) */
-	if (!off || time_after(jiffies, back_at + msecs_to_jiffies(INTEL_HDMI_HPD_BACK_MS)))
+	if (!time_after(jiffies, back_at + msecs_to_jiffies(INTEL_HDMI_HPD_BACK_MS)))
+		since_back = jiffies_to_msecs(jiffies - back_at);
+	else if (!repair)
 		return;
-	since_back = jiffies_to_msecs(jiffies - back_at);
 	if (READ_ONCE(connector->output_off) &&
 	    !time_after(jiffies, off_at + msecs_to_jiffies(INTEL_HDMI_HPD_BACK_MS)))
 		since_off = jiffies_to_msecs(jiffies - off_at);
@@ -3473,7 +3495,20 @@ static void intel_hdmi_relink_off(struct intel_connector *connector)
 	wait = intel_hdmi_relink_off_wait_ms(off, true, since_back, since_off);
 	if (wait)
 		msleep(wait);
-	if (since_off == UINT_MAX)
+	/* the link of this set up is a relink (INTEL_HDMI_RELINK_WATCH_MS) */
+	WRITE_ONCE(connector->relinked_at, jiffies);
+	WRITE_ONCE(connector->relinked, true);
+	if (!drop || since_back == UINT_MAX) {
+		if (since_off == UINT_MAX)
+			drm_info(display->drm,
+				 "[CONNECTOR:%d:%s] Repair of a link set up again after a drop of HPD: the link is set up %u ms later (hdmi_relink_off_ms)\n",
+				 connector->base.base.id, connector->base.name, wait);
+		else
+			drm_info(display->drm,
+				 "[CONNECTOR:%d:%s] Repair of a link set up again after a drop of HPD: the port was kept off %u ms more (off %u ms in all) before its link is set up again (hdmi_relink_off_ms)\n",
+				 connector->base.base.id, connector->base.name, wait,
+				 since_off + wait);
+	} else if (since_off == UINT_MAX)
 		drm_info(display->drm,
 			 "[CONNECTOR:%d:%s] HPD came back %u ms ago from a drop that no modeset of this output explains: the link is set up %u ms later, %u ms or more after HPD came back (hdmi_relink_off_ms)\n",
 			 connector->base.base.id, connector->base.name, since_back, wait, off);
@@ -4969,6 +5004,8 @@ static bool intel_hdmi_scdc_settle(struct intel_connector *connector, u8 config)
  * for 10 more passes at most: a commit that carries the connector at each
  * look (an HDR10+ vendor InfoFrame per scene or frame, HDR metadata, a mode)
  * left a sink whose TMDS_Config was reset after the hotplug unchecked.
+ * The same for the looks within INTEL_HDMI_RELINK_WATCH_MS of a relink
+ * (intel_ddi_hotplug(), intel_hdmi_scdc_settle.h).
  */
 #define HDMI_SCDC_LOOKS			4
 #define HDMI_SCDC_DEFERRED_LOOKS	10
@@ -4978,6 +5015,38 @@ static bool hdmi_scdc_look_again(int retries, bool deferred)
 	       (deferred && retries < HDMI_SCDC_LOOKS + HDMI_SCDC_DEFERRED_LOOKS);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Hades: the repair modeset of intel_hdmi_reset_link() keeps the port off first where the output was
+ * set up again after a relink less than INTEL_HDMI_RELINK_WATCH_MS ago (intel_hdmi_scdc_settle.h):
+ * the sink, an AV receiver still settling, reset its SCDC once more. What the sink says of the
+ * link it gets goes to the kernel log with it.
+ */
+static void intel_hdmi_relink_repair(struct intel_connector *connector)
+{
+	struct intel_display *display = to_intel_display(connector);
+	const unsigned int off = min_t(unsigned int, READ_ONCE(hdmi_relink_off_ms),
+				       INTEL_HDMI_RELINK_OFF_MAX_MS);
+	const long since_relink = intel_hdmi_since_relink(connector);
+	u8 flags, scrambler;
+
+	if (!intel_hdmi_relink_repair_due(off, since_relink))
+		return;
+	WRITE_ONCE(connector->relink_repair_due, true);
+
+	if (drm_scdc_readb(connector->base.ddc, SCDC_STATUS_FLAGS_0, &flags) < 0 ||
+	    drm_scdc_readb(connector->base.ddc, SCDC_SCRAMBLER_STATUS, &scrambler) < 0)
+		drm_info(display->drm,
+			 "[CONNECTOR:%d:%s] Sink's TMDS config lost %ld ms after its link was set up again after a drop of HPD (its status not read): the port is kept off %u ms first (hdmi_relink_off_ms)\n",
+			 connector->base.base.id, connector->base.name, since_relink, off);
+	else
+		drm_info(display->drm,
+			 "[CONNECTOR:%d:%s] Sink's TMDS config lost %ld ms after its link was set up again after a drop of HPD (its status: clock detected %s, channels 0/1/2 locked %s/%s/%s, scrambling seen %s): the port is kept off %u ms first (hdmi_relink_off_ms)\n",
+			 connector->base.base.id, connector->base.name, since_relink,
+			 str_yes_no(flags & SCDC_CLOCK_DETECT), str_yes_no(flags & SCDC_CH0_LOCK),
+			 str_yes_no(flags & SCDC_CH1_LOCK), str_yes_no(flags & SCDC_CH2_LOCK),
+			 str_yes_no(scrambler & SCDC_SCRAMBLING_STATUS), off);
+}
+
 static int intel_hdmi_reset_link(struct intel_encoder *encoder,
 				 struct drm_modeset_acquire_ctx *ctx)
 {
@@ -5083,7 +5152,12 @@ static int intel_hdmi_reset_link(struct intel_encoder *encoder,
 		 connector->base.base.id, connector->base.name, config,
 		 str_yes_no(crtc_state->hdmi_scrambling),
 		 crtc_state->hdmi_high_tmds_clock_ratio ? 40 : 10);
-	return intel_modeset_commit_pipes(display, BIT(crtc->pipe), ctx);
+	/* Hades: with the port kept off first, shortly after a relink (intel_hdmi_scdc_settle.h) */
+	intel_hdmi_relink_repair(connector);
+	ret = intel_modeset_commit_pipes(display, BIT(crtc->pipe), ctx);
+	/* (the commit is blocking: its set up has taken the flag, or there was none) */
+	WRITE_ONCE(connector->relink_repair_due, false);
+	return ret;
 }
 
 static void intel_ddi_link_check(struct intel_encoder *encoder)
@@ -5183,7 +5257,9 @@ intel_ddi_hotplug(struct intel_encoder *encoder,
 		connector->base.connector_type == DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_HDMIA &&
 		connector->base.status == connector_status_connected &&
 		hdmi_scdc_look_again(connector->hotplug_retries,
-				     connector->hdmi_scdc_deferred);
+				     connector->hdmi_scdc_deferred ||
+				     /* Hades: and after a relink (intel_hdmi_scdc_settle.h) */
+				     intel_hdmi_relink_watching(intel_hdmi_since_relink(connector)));
 	if (scdc_recheck && connector->hdmi_scdc_deferred &&
 	    !connector->hdmi_scdc_recheck &&
 	    connector->base.status == connector_status_connected)
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_display_types.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_display_types.h
index 99c6587..7f8de31 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_display_types.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_display_types.h
@@ -656,6 +656,15 @@ struct intel_connector {
 	bool relink_off_due;
 	bool output_off;
 	unsigned long output_off_at;
+	/*
+	 * Hades: i915.hdmi_relink_off_ms after a relink (INTEL_HDMI_RELINK_WATCH_MS): the output was
+	 * last set up after its port was kept off at relinked_at (relinked, intel_hdmi_relink_off()),
+	 * and the repair modeset of intel_hdmi_reset_link() under way keeps the port off as well
+	 * (relink_repair_due)
+	 */
+	bool relinked;
+	bool relink_repair_due;
+	unsigned long relinked_at;
 
 	/* since POLL and HPD connectors may use the same HPD line keep the native
 	   state of connector->polled in case hotplug storm detection changes it */
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_hdmi_scdc_settle.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_hdmi_scdc_settle.h
index ffc9c3a..764a26f 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_hdmi_scdc_settle.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_hdmi_scdc_settle.h
@@ -80,8 +80,8 @@ static inline bool intel_hdmi_scdc_settle_waits(unsigned int settle_ms, bool bac
  * How long the output waits before its link is set up again, in ms (0: not at all):
  * @off_ms: i915.hdmi_relink_off_ms (0: never; above INTEL_HDMI_RELINK_OFF_MAX_MS, that)
  * @due: HPD came back from a drop that no modeset of the output explains, and the output has not
- *       been set up since
- * @since_back_ms: since HPD came back
+ *       been set up since; or a repair modeset after a relink (intel_hdmi_relink_repair_due())
+ * @since_back_ms: since HPD came back (UINT_MAX: long ago)
  * @since_off_ms: since the port was last turned off (UINT_MAX: never on, or long ago)
  */
 static inline unsigned int intel_hdmi_relink_off_wait_ms(unsigned int off_ms, bool due,
@@ -101,4 +101,46 @@ static inline unsigned int intel_hdmi_relink_off_wait_ms(unsigned int off_ms, bo
 	return wait;
 }
 
+/*
+ * i915.hdmi_relink_off_ms after a relink, issue #28 with Hades 1.2: the port kept off before the link
+ * is set up again brought the AVM 90's picture back, but not every time, at 300 ms and at 1000 ms
+ * alike. Each failure had the same pattern, and no good case had it: a few seconds after the link
+ * came back (the relink; 2.2 s in the log of the report), a later look of intel_ddi_hotplug() read
+ * the sink's TMDS_Config as 0x00 again, and the repair modeset of intel_hdmi_reset_link() went out
+ * with no time off; the AVM then showed no picture until the output was turned off for 0.3 s and on
+ * again (DPMS), which brought it back at once. While it settles, the AVM's SCDC can read as reset
+ * once more, and the repair of that needs what the first one needed: the TMDS clock stopped for a
+ * moment.
+ *
+ * So for INTEL_HDMI_RELINK_WATCH_MS after a relink, a repair modeset of intel_hdmi_reset_link()
+ * keeps the port off as well (intel_hdmi_relink_off_wait_ms() with @due), and intel_ddi_hotplug()
+ * goes on looking at the sink's SCDC once a second until that time is up (within the most looks
+ * after a hotplug that hdmi_scdc_look_again() allows), so that a reset after a repair made near
+ * the end of the looks is seen as well. Each repair with the port kept off is a relink, and starts
+ * the time again; the cap of intel_hdmi_reset_link() (3 modesets in 20 s) still holds. A repair
+ * that no relink came shortly before (an LG G5 whose drop answers a modeset of the output, or a
+ * sink that never drops HPD) and every mode set asked by user space are as before. 5 s: twice the
+ * reset seen (2.2 s after the relink), and the look after it.
+ */
+#define INTEL_HDMI_RELINK_WATCH_MS	5000
+
+/*
+ * The output was set up again after a relink less than INTEL_HDMI_RELINK_WATCH_MS ago:
+ * @since_relink_ms: since then (negative: no relink, or one too long ago to be known)
+ */
+static inline bool intel_hdmi_relink_watching(long since_relink_ms)
+{
+	return since_relink_ms >= 0 && since_relink_ms < INTEL_HDMI_RELINK_WATCH_MS;
+}
+
+/*
+ * The repair modeset of intel_hdmi_reset_link() keeps the port off first, as a relink does:
+ * @off_ms: i915.hdmi_relink_off_ms (0: never)
+ * @since_relink_ms: as for intel_hdmi_relink_watching()
+ */
+static inline bool intel_hdmi_relink_repair_due(unsigned int off_ms, long since_relink_ms)
+{
+	return off_ms && intel_hdmi_relink_watching(since_relink_ms);
+}
+
 #endif /* __INTEL_HDMI_SCDC_SETTLE_H__ */
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/tests/drm_hdmi_scdc_settle_test.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/tests/drm_hdmi_scdc_settle_test.c
index ae83ff8..ebfa75e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/tests/drm_hdmi_scdc_settle_test.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/tests/drm_hdmi_scdc_settle_test.c
@@ -105,11 +105,61 @@ static void drm_test_scdc_relink_off(struct kunit *test)
 			300);
 }
 
+/*
+ * i915.hdmi_relink_off_ms after a relink: a sink that lost its TMDS config again shortly after its
+ * link was set up again with the port kept off has its repair with the port kept off as well
+ */
+static void drm_test_scdc_relink_repair(struct kunit *test)
+{
+	/* no relink, or one too long ago: as before */
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_FALSE(test, intel_hdmi_relink_watching(-1));
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_FALSE(test, intel_hdmi_relink_watching(INTEL_HDMI_RELINK_WATCH_MS));
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_FALSE(test, intel_hdmi_relink_repair_due(300, -1));
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_FALSE(test, intel_hdmi_relink_repair_due(300, INTEL_HDMI_RELINK_WATCH_MS));
+	/* the parameter off: nothing, as in 1.1 */
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_FALSE(test, intel_hdmi_relink_repair_due(0, 2160));
+	/* from the relink itself to the end of the watch */
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_TRUE(test, intel_hdmi_relink_watching(0));
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_TRUE(test, intel_hdmi_relink_repair_due(300, 0));
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_TRUE(test, intel_hdmi_relink_repair_due(300, INTEL_HDMI_RELINK_WATCH_MS - 1));
+	/*
+	 * issue #28 with 1.2 at 1000 ms (uptime 2368.86 the relink, 2371.02 TMDS_Config 0x00 again):
+	 * the repair 2160 ms after the relink, the port turned off 4 ms before its set up, stays off
+	 * 1000 ms; HPD came back long before
+	 */
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test,
+			intel_hdmi_relink_off_wait_ms(1000, intel_hdmi_relink_repair_due(1000, 2160),
+						      UINT_MAX, 4),
+			996);
+	/* ... and at 300 ms */
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test,
+			intel_hdmi_relink_off_wait_ms(300, intel_hdmi_relink_repair_due(300, 2160),
+						      4300, 4),
+			296);
+	/* where the sink dropped HPD again and it came back just now: HPD back that long as well */
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test,
+			intel_hdmi_relink_off_wait_ms(300, intel_hdmi_relink_repair_due(300, 2160), 60, 4),
+			296);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test,
+			intel_hdmi_relink_off_wait_ms(300, intel_hdmi_relink_repair_due(300, 2160), 10, 200),
+			290);
+	/*
+	 * the looks go on after a repair near the end of the looks of the hotplug: a reset as late as
+	 * the latest seen (2.2 s) is seen at the look after it
+	 */
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_TRUE(test, intel_hdmi_relink_watching(2200 + 1000));
+	/* an LG G5, never relinked (its drops answer a modeset of the output): its repair at once */
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test,
+			intel_hdmi_relink_off_wait_ms(300, intel_hdmi_relink_repair_due(300, -1), 60, 4),
+			0);
+}
+
 static struct kunit_case drm_hdmi_scdc_settle_tests[] = {
 	KUNIT_CASE(drm_test_scdc_settle_answers),
 	KUNIT_CASE(drm_test_scdc_settle_waits),
 	KUNIT_CASE(drm_test_scdc_settle_looks),
 	KUNIT_CASE(drm_test_scdc_relink_off),
+	KUNIT_CASE(drm_test_scdc_relink_repair),
 	{ }
 };
 
-- 
2.53.0

